{"name":"Karaka","hex":"#2d2d24","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"karaka","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree, Corynocarpus laevigatus, bearing fruits with a kernel that can be eaten after extensive roasting and washing."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A significator."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/karaka"}],"entries":[{"title":"Corynocarpus laevigatus","blocks":[{"text":"Corynocarpus laevigatus, commonly known as karaka or the New Zealand laurel, is an evergreen tree in the family Corynocarpaceae. It is endemic to New Zealand and is common throughout the North Island and less common in the South Island. C. laevigatus individuals are also found on the Chatham Islands, Kermadec Islands, and the Three Kings Islands. C. laevigatus is mainly a coastal tree, although in the North Island, it is also found inland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Karaka_in_Raupo_Bay%2C_Banks_Peninsula_%28New_Zealand%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Karaka_in_Raupo_Bay%2C_Banks_Peninsula_%28New_Zealand%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corynocarpus_laevigatus","wikidata":"Q5477982"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Karaka_in_Raupo_Bay%2C_Banks_Peninsula_%28New_Zealand%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Karaka_in_Raupo_Bay%2C_Banks_Peninsula_%28New_Zealand%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Karaka_in_Raupo_Bay%2C_Banks_Peninsula_%28New_Zealand%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Karaka_in_Raupo_Bay%2C_Banks_Peninsula_%28New_Zealand%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Karaka_in_Raupo_Bay%2C_Banks_Peninsula_%28New_Zealand%29_%28cropped%